  <div class="wrap story-inner">
    <header class="story-heading">
      <span class="story-label">Our story</span>
      <h2 id="community-story-heading">How GHL Bangladesh began.</h2>
      <p class="story-byline">A note from Mehedi Sharif</p>
      <p class="story-credit">
        Co-organised by Mehedi Sharif and <a
          href="https://www.facebook.com/vidmshariful"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          aria-label="Shariful Islam on Facebook (opens in a new tab)"
          >Shariful Islam</a
        >
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="story-copy">
      <p>
        Shariful Islam and I kept coming back to the same thought: so many
        people in Bangladesh work with GoHighLevel every day, yet we hardly ever
        meet in person. We wanted to change that. The idea was simple: bring GHL
        users into one room and let them share what was actually working for
        them.
      </p>
      <p>
        On <time datetime="2026-06-11">June 11, 2026</time>, I had the honour of
        co-organising GHL Bangladesh MeetUp 2026 with Shariful. It was an
        unofficial, community-driven meetup. Nothing fancy, just people who use
        GHL sitting together, sharing their experiences, and talking face to
        face about the work they do every day.
      </p>
      <p>
        I didn’t expect the room to fill up the way it did. The speakers were
        open about their real experiences, people asked great questions, and the
        conversations felt genuine. Seeing that response brought me back to why
        we had wanted to organise the meetup in the first place: there were
        people here with experiences worth sharing.
      </p>
      <p>
        Shariful and I organised this meetup together, and I’m grateful to him
        for helping make it happen. Those conversations between us became a
        chance for a wider community to meet. For me, that is what GHL
        Bangladesh is about: putting faces to names, asking questions, and
        learning from people doing the same work.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

